Subject: [PATCH] dtype: prefer F32 over the F16 fallback on non-CUDA devices

Fixes NaN/Inf logits ("Invalid sampling probability at index 0: NaN") for large
GGUF models (e.g. Qwen3-14B) on GPUs without bfloat16 support, such as Intel
Macs running Metal.

Root cause: `determine_auto_dtype_all` probes BF16 -> F16 -> F32 and returns the
first that supports a trivial matmul. On a device without hardware bf16 the BF16
probe fails and F16 is selected. GGUF attention materialises the Q*K^T score
matrix in the compute dtype (eager `naive_sdpa`, and the Metal fused
`candle_nn::ops::sdpa` used for prefill). F16's max is 65504; the 14B model's
scaled scores exceed it -> Inf -> NaN after softmax, which the sampler rejects.

Fix: on non-CUDA devices, drop F16 from the auto candidates (BF16 -> F32). BF16
has F32's exponent range and F32 is safe; only F16 overflows. CUDA is unchanged
(flash-attention accumulates softmax in F32).

Apply in the onde-mistralrs fork, then publish onde-mistralrs 0.8.3 and bump the
dependency in onde. The published crate ships this file as src/utils/normal.rs;
the path below uses the fork's workspace directory.

--- a/mistralrs-core/src/utils/normal.rs
+++ b/mistralrs-core/src/utils/normal.rs
@@ -134,7 +134,18 @@
     #[cfg(not(any(feature = "accelerate", target_os = "ios")))]
     {
         let dev_dtypes = get_dtypes();
-        for dtype in get_dtypes_non_cuda()
+        // Prefer F32 over F16 on non-CUDA devices (Metal / CPU). The eager
+        // (`naive_sdpa`) and Metal fused-SDPA attention paths materialise the
+        // attention score matrix in the compute dtype, and large models
+        // (e.g. Qwen3-14B) overflow F16's 65504 maximum -> Inf -> NaN logits.
+        // BF16 (same exponent range as F32) and F32 are safe; F16 is not.
+        // CUDA keeps F16 because flash-attention accumulates softmax in F32.
+        let candidate_dtypes: Vec<DType> = if devices.iter().any(|d| d.is_cuda()) {
+            get_dtypes_non_cuda() // [BF16, F16]
+        } else {
+            vec![DType::BF16] // BF16, else fall through to F32 below
+        };
+        for dtype in candidate_dtypes
             .iter()
             .filter(|x| dev_dtypes.contains(x))
         {
